        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474-a1">

                <pb facs="0683" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg595"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 547.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Bowen to Mr.
                            Newberry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bible House</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Newberry</hi>: Another seizure of Bibles has
                    occurred. It occurred three days ago at Geybize, a town a little ways out on the
                    Nicomedian Railway, within the limits of the vilayet of Constantinople. As I
                    understand the matter, the personal liberty of the colporteur has not been
                    interfered with, but only his books seized. The only excuse is that they have
                    not the imprimatur of the Turkish Government. But as they were not printed in
                    Turkey it is not surprising that this imprimatur should be missing. They are
                    Bibles which come through the customhouse in the regular way, and which are in
                    circulation all over the Empire. It ought to be easy for his excellency to
                    settle the case, as it is so near headquarters. As I do not wish our agent
                    delayed long in this small town, I hope you may be able to request that the
                    books be given back as soon as possible. I am perfectly disgusted that this
                    thing should occur right here and that I should be obliged to come to you so
                    soon again with a request of this nature, but I seem to be left with no choice
                    in the matter.</p>
                <p>I am etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Bowen</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Agent of the American Bible
                    Society.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
